# TypeScript Standards

- Strict mode enabled everywhere (`"strict": true`)
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow with type guards or Zod `.parse()`
- Prefer `type` over `interface`; use `interface` only when intentional extension is needed
- All exported functions must have explicit return types
- Zod schemas in `packages/shared` are the **single source of truth** — infer TypeScript types from them

```typescript
// ✅ Good — derive type from schema
import { CharacterSchema } from '@ironquill/shared';
export type Character = z.infer<typeof CharacterSchema>;

// ❌ Bad — manually duplicating the schema
export interface Character {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  // ...
}
```

- Use discriminated unions for state modelling

```typescript
// ✅ Good
type SessionState =
  | { status: 'idle' }
  | { status: 'loading' }
  | { status: 'active'; sessionId: string }
  | { status: 'error'; message: string };
```

- Never cast with `as` unless at a verified boundary (e.g. Drizzle JSONB `.$type<T>()`)
